  "stamp",
  "showcase"
 ],
 "teaches": [
  "Run a swipe without touchExpression: onTouchDown stores touchX(), touchY() and animationTime(); the card follows touchX() - downX while @drag is 1",
  "Decide fling or spring at release in onTouchUp from the gesture alone: speed = distance / max(time held, 0.04), dismiss when |dx| > 110 or (speed > 700 and |dx| > 36), and store the direction, the release offset and upT = animationTime()",
  "Spring back with a damped oscillator of the time since release: offset · e^(-7t) · (cos 13t + 0.54 sin 13t), and fly off with x = release + dir · (v·t + 2600 t²)",
  "Draw a stack with one loop: i = 0..3 is depth 2, 1, 0 and the card in flight; each depth's scale, offset and dimming come from k + a shared lift that follows the drag (and finishes after a fling)",
  "Paint five different scenes from one body: per-card float arrays drive layer alphas (night, warm, day skies, aurora, sea, landmarks) and ridge parameters for pathExpression",
  "Close a pathExpression ridge to the bottom by running a[0] slightly past 0..1 with x clamped and y = ifElse(card height, ridge, inside)",
  "Fire wakeIn only while a card moves: 0.016 + 3600 · step(t, 1.4)"
 ],
 "pitfalls": [
  "Modifier actions are parsed before the canvas commands and cannot read tree variables (componentWidth(), touchExpression values): keep the gesture state in root variables and do geometry in the tree",
  "The notch stop modes of touchExpression need touchSpec, which the Java JSON parser drops, and a notched touch value cannot be reset by the document: this is why the stack uses actions and time instead",
  "touchVelX() is only loaded by the C++ player at touch-up (not Java, not TS): measure the speed yourself",
  "A button tap also reaches the canvas behind it (TS), so the canvas's touch-up only commits when the finger moved more than 8 px",
  "step(x, edge) is strict: step(1, 1) is 0, so test a direction with step(@dir, 0.5)",
  "A computed colour is evaluated once per frame, not per loop iteration: vary paint alpha and gradients by the loop index instead",
  "Taps are ignored for 0.3 s after a fling so two cards are never in flight",
  "Java's addDataList drops the list id, so textLookup cannot reach it from JSON: each card's texts are five drawTextAnchored per field, the right one shown by alpha 1 - min(1, |c - j|)"
 ],
